wHI8fAO|fc_0344e99872bb989d016a920195794087d284e5ee164e0de7ee", "name": "bash", "arguments": {"command": "git status --short && find tests/src/org.springframework/spring-core/5.3.15/build/natively-collected -name 'reachability-metadata.json' -print | sort"}}], "api": "openai-codex-responses", "provider": "openai-codex", "model": "gpt-5.6-terra", "usage": {"input": 3024, "output": 380, "cacheRead": 36352, "cacheWrite": 0, "reasoning": 147, "totalTokens": 39756, "cost": {"input": 0, "output": 0, "cacheRead": 0, "cacheWrite": 0, "total": 0}}, "stopReason": "toolUse", "timestamp": 1787953549401, "responseId": "resp_0344e99872bb989d016a92018dcfec87d28bcb3c69e2412c6a", "rawStopReason": "completed"}, "toolResults": [{"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_WO7F7wlFDaiIEeUE9hmlBXhG|fc_0344e99872bb989d016a920195791c87d2a9cad06802ff06b5", "toolName": "bash", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "tests/src/org.springframework/spring-core/5.3.15/src/test/resources/META-INF/native-image/reachability-metadata.json:52:        \"typeReached\" : \"org_springframework.spring_core.ReflectUtilsTest\"\ntests/src/org.springframework/spring-core/5.3.15/src/test/resources/META-INF/native-image/reachability-metadata.json:58:        \"typeReached\" : \"org_springframework.spring_core.ReflectUtilsTest\"\ntests/src/org.springframework/spring-core/5.3.15/src/test/resources/META-INF/native-image/reachability-metadata.json:91:        \"typeReached\" : \"org_springframework.spring_core.ReflectUtilsTest\"\ntests/src/org.springframework/spring-core/5.3.15/src/test/resources/META-INF/native-image/reachability-metadata.json:103:        \"typeReached\" : \"org_springframework.spring_core.ReflectUtilsTest\"\ntests/src/org.springframework/spring-core/5.3.15/src/test/java/org_springframework/spring_core/ReflectUtilsTest.java:24:public class ReflectUtilsTest {\n\n\nCommand exited with code 1"}], "details": {}, "isError": true, "timestamp": 1787953558347}, {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_pNZ3nS9dqt8gygWsPghlZ3Bj|fc_0344e99872bb989d016a920195793087d2bc5a8397a09c34ab", "toolName": "read", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "# FS-tests: The `tests/` suite\n\n[`tests/`](../../tests) is what justifies every byte of shipped metadata. A\nmetadata entry exists only because a test exercises the dynamic access it\nregisters and would fail without it (§GOAL-tested-metadata); this suite holds\nthose tests. The behavioral requirements for tests are normative in\n§FS-repository-functional-spec.5.2 and, point by point, in §FS-test-contract;\nthis document describes the test-project contract.\n\n## 1. Coordinate test projects\n\n- [`tests/src/<groupId>/<artifactId>/<version>/`](../../tests/src) — one\n  self-contained Gradle test project per coordinate, unless an `index.json`\n  entry sets `test-version` to share one suite across versions. Each project\n  exercises the library's reachable surface through its public API, declares any\n  Docker images it needs in `required-docker-images.txt`, and is the unit the\n  harness runs on the JVM and on `native-image`.\n- `src/test/resources/META-INF/native-image/reachability-metadata.json`\n  — when present, the test-only reachability metadata that\n  `splitTestOnlyMetadata` carved out of the shipped library metadata so the test\n  image can reach its own helper types without those entries reaching consumers\n  (§FS-metadata, §FS-repository-functional-spec.5.1).\n- `build.gradle` may add test dependencies and, when there is no better public\n  API path, restrict Native Image configuration edits to `--add-opens` /\n  `--add-exports` under `graalvmNative`.\n- Test assertions use standard Java or library exceptions, not Gradle-only\n  failure types such as `GradleException`.\n\n## 2. What a good test must do\n\nA good test drives the library the way a real consumer would, so that a missing\nor wrong metadata entry makes it fail. The requirements are normative in\n§FS-repository-functional-spec.5.2 and §FS-test-contract; the rules below are a\nsummary of what they mean when writing one.\n\n- **Drive real behavior through the public API.** Exercise enough of the\n  library's reachable surface that the test fails when metadata is wrong or\n  missing. Do not reach for reflection directly unless the public API genuinely\n  requires it, and keep tests outside the library's own packages — a test must\n  not live in a library package just to touch package-private or internal code.\n- **Test supported behavior, not bugs.** Target behavior the library actually\n  supports. Never make an uncovered dynamic-access call site \"covered\" by\n  asserting a known bug, regression, or version-specific failure; exception\n  assertions are acceptable only for documented, supported negative-path APIs.\n- **Stay version-agnostic.** Do not pin to a specific library version or hardcode\n  the artifact version in inputs or assertions. Scaffold-only tests that do not\n  actually exercise the library are not acceptable.\n- **Don't fake the library.** No source stubs, fake replacements, or shadow\n  classes for library or dependency types in their real packages. If a needed API\n  is missing from the test classpath, add the correct test dependency or leave\n  the call site unreached with an explanation — never paper over it.\n- **Run under Native Image by default.** Tests execute on `native-image`, not\n  only the JVM; do not disable native execution with `@DisabledInNativeImage`,\n  `assumeFalse(...)`, `isNativeImageRuntime()`, or equivalent guards. When a test\n  genuinely needs open-ended dynamic class loading that Native Image cannot\n  support, prove it fails for the right reason — catch `Error` and verify it with\n  `NativeImageSupport.isUnsupportedFeatureError(e)` — rather than skipping it.\n- **Be deterministic, isolated, and bounded.** No network except against a\n  declared, pre-pulled `allowed-docker-image` with networking disabled, and\n  per-coordinate runs must not depend on or affect other coordinates\n  (§FS-repository-functional-spec.6). Each individual test completes in under\n  60 seconds, using bounded waits and closing every client, server, and executor\n  it opens.\n- **Keep test code original.** Do not copy upstream or other third-party test\n  sources into this repository. Upstream tests may be used only as behavioral\n  examples, and documentation only as API guidance. Review policy details live\n  in [REVIEWING.md](../REVIEWING.md); what review may block on — rule strength,\n  shape limits, coverage gates, and cheating patterns — is normative in\n  §FS-contribution-contract.\n\n## 3. How the suite is exercised\n\nThe harness compiles and runs each coordinate's project through the\n`compileTestJava` → `javaTest` → `nativeTestCompile` → `nativeTest` lanes\n(§AR-test-harness.3), and CI runs the same lanes across the `ci.json` JDK/OS\nmatrix and native-image modes (§AR-repository-ci). A version is recorded as\nsupported only after it passes on every required environment, and dynamic-access\ncoverage between consecutive versions must not regress\n(§FS-repository-functional-spec.5.2, §GOAL-protect-shipped-metadata). New test\nprojects are created from the scaffold templates by the authoring tasks\n(§AR-test-harness.5), by a human or by Forge (§forge/FS-forge-functional-spec).\n"}], "isError": false, "timestamp": 1787953558348}, {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_BXFPU4IPMuzJl6wKHHfBP6df|fc_0344e99872bb989d016a920195793887d2ab268104f3705d4d", "toolName": "bash", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "docs/functional-spec/contribution-contract.md:154:   `catch (Error)` without the `isUnsupportedFeatureError` verification, and\ndocs/functional-spec/contribution-contract.md:155:   the sanctioned pattern applied outside genuine open-ended dynamic class\ndocs/functional-spec/test-contract.md:319:      instead of exercising it (and needs runtime bytecode generation, §FS-test-contract.4.5).\ndocs/functional-spec/test-contract.md:373:reachability metadata or unsupported behavior — exactly what this repository\ndocs/functional-spec/test-contract.md:406:### 4.3 The sole sanctioned exception: open-ended dynamic class loading\ndocs/functional-spec/test-contract.md:409:that fundamentally requires open-ended dynamic class loading Native Image\ndocs/functional-spec/test-contract.md:410:cannot support: loading classes, JARs, generated bytecode, plugin\ndocs/functional-spec/test-contract.md:414:`NativeImageSupport.isUnsupportedFeatureError(e)` from\ndocs/functional-spec/test-contract.md:422:    if (!NativeImageSupport.isUnsupportedFeatureError(e)) {\ndocs/functional-spec/test-contract.md:454:Tests do not target behavior that depends on runtime bytecode generation,\ndocs/functional-spec/test-contract.md:455:runtime class definition or loading, runtime lambda definition, Java agent\ndocs/functional-spec/test-contract.md:457:URL/plugin/OSGi class loader paths, custom class loaders that introduce classes\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md:29:> **Adding this repository to a user's build must never change how the user's code runs.** The metadata is purely additive — it can only fill in registrations `native-image` would otherwise miss; it cannot alter class initialization, replace user bytecode, or execute code at image-build time.\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md:34:- **No library patching.** No substitutions, bytecode rewrites, or shaded forks of upstream libraries. Patching ships a different version than the one the user resolved through Maven Central, is invisible at the dependency-resolution layer, and is unstable across upstream releases.\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md:114:| `library-unsupported-version` | Issue | Compatibility automation found a newer upstream library version that is not currently supported by the existing metadata and tests. |\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md:444:<group:artifact:version>` and the labels are `library-unsupported-version` plus\ndocs/functional-spec/tests.md:55:  genuinely needs open-ended dynamic class loading that Native Image cannot\ndocs/functional-spec/tests.md:57:  `NativeImageSupport.isUnsupportedFeatureError(e)` — rather than skipping it.\ntests/tck-build-logic/src/main/java/org/graalvm/internal/tck/utils/BaseLayerUtils.java:43:            \"jdk.unsupported\",\ntests/tck-build-logic/src/main/java/org/graalvm/internal/tck/utils/MetadataEntryOwnership.java:96:            if (type.has(\"lambda\")) {\ntests/tck-build-logic/src/main/java/org/graalvm/internal/tck/utils/MetadataEntryOwnership.java:97:                return type.get(\"lambda\").toString();\ntests/tck-build-logic/src/main/java/org/graalvm/internal/tck/stats/LibraryStatsSupport.java:151:            throw new GradleException(\"Unsupported library stats metric '\" + metric + \"'. Supported metrics: \" + DYNAMIC_ACCESSES_METRIC);\ntests/tck-build-logic/src/main/java/org/graalvm/internal/tck/stats/LibraryStatsSupport.java:604:    /// data-driven — no jar bytecode scanning.\ntests/tck-build-logic/src/main/java/org/graalvm/internal/tck/stats/LibraryStatsSupport.java:1025:                \"Unsupported dynamic access report type '\" + rawType + \"' in \" + path\ntests/tck-build-logic/src/main/java/org/graalvm/internal/tck/ScaffoldTask.java:419:                throw new IllegalStateException(\"Unsupported Scala version for scaffold generation: \" + language.version());\ntests/tck-build-logic/src/main/java/org/graalvm/internal/tck/ScaffoldTask.java:421:            throw new IllegalStateException(\"Unsupported language for scaffold generation: \" + language.name());\ntests/tck-build-logic/src/main/groovy/org/graalvm/internal/tck/harness/tasks/AbstractLibraryStatsTask.java:212:        // When library JARs contain no bytecode (no .class files), JaCoCo has nothing\ntests/tck-build-logic/src/main/groovy/org/graalvm/internal/tck/harness/tasks/AbstractLibraryStatsTask.java:217:                    \"Library JARs for {} contain no bytecode. Writing empty dynamic access stats and N/A coverage.\",\ntests/src/org.springframework/spring-core/5.3.15/src/test/java/org_springframework/spring_core/AbstractClassLoaderTest.java:15:/** Verifies CGLIB's public transforming class loader selection behavior. */\ntests/src/org.springframework/spring-core/5.3.15/src/test/java/org_springframework/spring_core/OverridingClassLoaderTest.java:14:/** Verifies Spring's public overriding class loader behavior. */\ntests/src/org.springframework/spring-core/5.3.15/src/test/java/org_springframework/spring_core/PathMatchingResourcePatternResolverTest.java:17:/** Verifies classpath resource discovery with explicit and system class loaders. */\n"}], "isError": false, "timestamp": 1787953558348}, {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_dJXj33jUiTjB3BJ6PwHI8fAO|fc_0344e99872bb989d016a920195794087d284e5ee164e0de7ee", "toolName": "bash", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "tests/src/org.springframework/spring-core/5.3.15/build/natively-collected/_global_/agent/reachability-metadata.json\ntests/src/org.springframework/spring-core/5.3.15/build/natively-collected/runs/cycle-0/reachability-metadata.json\ntests/src/org.springframework/spring-core/5.3.15/build/natively-collected/runs/cycle-1/reachability-metadata.json\ntests/src/org.springframework/spring-core/5.3.15/build/natively-collected/runs/cycle-2/reachability-metadata.json\ntests/src/org.springframework/spring-core/5.3.15/build/natively-collected/runs/cycle-3/reachability-metadata.json\ntests/src/org.springframework/spring-core/5.3.15/build/natively-collected/runs/cycle-4/reachability-metadata.json\ntests/src/org.springframework/spring-core/5.3.15/build/natively-collected/runs/cycle-5/reachability-metadata.json\ntests/src/org.springframework/spring-core/5.3.15/build/natively-collected/runs/cycle-6/reachability-metadata.json\n"}], "isError": false, "timestamp": 1787953558348}]}
